{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.CoulombCharge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.CoulombCharge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":20,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.mirror_odd_neutral_neutron_forces_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.mirror_odd_neutral_neutron_forces_zero","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L195-L204","doc":"**Neutron neutrality forces every quark charge to vanish.**\n\nSo the mechanism cannot hold a neutral neutron beside a charged proton:\ndemanding the first makes the second neutral too. The Standard Model\nescapes this because it takes `|Q_u| = 2|Q_d|`, an asymmetry between the\ntwo orientations that a pure mirror cannot supply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.neutron_charge_eq_neg_proton_charge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.neutron_charge_eq_neg_proton_charge","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L185-L193","doc":"**A mirror-odd charge makes the neutron the proton's exact opposite.**\n\nWith the proton `uud` and the neutron `udd`, oddness alone gives\n`Q(n) = −Q(p)`. Nothing about crossing counts, `q`, or the particular\ncharge formula enters. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.asserted_quark_charges_not_mirror_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.asserted_quark_charges_not_mirror_odd","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L174-L183","doc":"**The asserted pair `(+2/3, −1/3)` is not a mirror pair.**\n\nThe two blocks state a mechanism that forces `Q(d) = −Q(u)` and then\nassert a pair whose ratio is `−2`. No crossing count repairs this: it is\na statement about the symmetry, not about the counts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.abs_value_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.abs_value_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":168,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L168-L172","doc":"A mirror pair carries equal magnitudes, so its charge ratio is `-1` for\nevery crossing count. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.value_mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.value_mirror","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L161-L166","doc":"**`Q` is odd under the mirror.** This is the invariant the whole\nobstruction rests on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.mirror","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.mirror","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L157-L159","doc":"Reversing every crossing: the mirror of a braid word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.antisymCoefficient_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.antisymCoefficient_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L124-L141","doc":"The Coulomb coefficient vanishes only for the empty braid word — not on\nthe `n₊ = n₋` locus, which annihilates the SYMMETRIC channel instead. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.antisymCoefficient_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.antisymCoefficient_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L112-L122","doc":"**The Coulomb coefficient is never negative.**\n\nThis is the falsifiable consequence of the corrected assignment, and it\nis why `Q` cannot be read as an electric charge on the strength of this\ndecomposition alone: the antisymmetric channel admits no attractive\nsign, so the trichotomy `Q ≶ 0 ↦ repulsive/attractive` that this block\npreviously asserted has no representative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.coulombContribution_antisymmetric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.coulombContribution_antisymmetric","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L104-L110","doc":"The Coulomb contribution is antisymmetric under q ↔ q⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.coulombContribution_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.coulombContribution_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L98-L102","doc":"The Coulomb contribution vanishes at q = 1 (undeformed limit). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.strongContribution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.strongContribution","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L92-L96","doc":"The symmetric (strong) contribution: Q(H) · (q + q⁻¹).\n`Q` — the halved writhe — is the coefficient of THIS channel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.coulombContribution","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.coulombContribution","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L87-L90","doc":"The Coulomb (antisymmetric) contribution: ½(n₊ + n₋)(q − q⁻¹). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.antisymCoefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.antisymCoefficient","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L74-L85","doc":"The coefficient of the ANTISYMMETRIC (Coulomb) channel: ½(n₊ + n₋).\n\n**CORRECTED 2026-08-29 (bean `qou-toul`).** This file previously\ndefined `coulombCorrection = value * (q − q⁻¹)`, i.e. it multiplied the\nhalved *writhe* `Q` into the antisymmetric channel. That is the swapped\nassignment: by `prop:crossing-energy-decomposition` the antisymmetric\n`sinh` weight is blind to the crossing sign, so its multiplicity is the\ncrossing COUNT, and `Q` is the coefficient of the symmetric channel.\n`QOU.Braiding.CrossingEnergy.swapped_decomposition_off_by` states the\nfailure quantitatively. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.neutral_iff_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.neutral_iff_zero","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L55-L72","doc":"Neutral composites have zero Coulomb charge. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.isNeutral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.isNeutral","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L50-L53","doc":"A composite is electromagnetically neutral when Q(H) = 0,\ni.e., n₊ = n₋. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.value","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L46-L48","doc":"The Coulomb charge value: Q = (n₊ − n₋) / 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.numNegative","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.numNegative","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Number of negative crossings n₋. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.numPositive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.numPositive","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Number of positive crossings n₊. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Braiding.CoulombCharge","kind":"structure","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.lean#L30-L44","doc":"**Coulomb charge** of a knot composite with braid word β.\n\nQ(H) = ½(n₊(β) − n₋(β))\n\nwhere n₊, n₋ are the positive and negative crossing counts.\n\n- Q(H) > 0: net positive crossings, repulsive Coulomb contribution.\n- Q(H) = 0: electromagnetically neutral.\n- Q(H) < 0: net negative crossings, attractive Coulomb contribution. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:coulomb-charge","label":"def:coulomb-charge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/coulomb-charge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}